[s0l0!-header][h1]Creating Classes[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

In order to create your own custom objects, you must first create the corresponding classes. This is accomplished by right clicking on the [b]src [/b]folder in Eclipse and selecting Create->New->Class. Give your class a name and click [b]Finish [/b]to add the new class to your project: [img id="2866" width="100%"]
As you can see, Eclipse has already added the initial code for the class.
Now lets create a simple method in our new class.
[b][u]Animal.java[/u][/b] [code format="java" ]public class Animal {
  void bark() {
    System.out.println("Woof-Woof");
  }
}[/code]
We declared a [b]bark()[/b] method in our [b]Animal [/b]class.
[note]Now, in order to use the class and it's methods, we need to declare an [b]object [/b]of that class.[/note]

